## Context Block 1 — Architecture

There are two kill chain implementations. `backend/app/signals/kill_chain.py` is the **active scorer** wired into `/api/v1/signals` (via `compute_kill_chain`). `live_monitoring/enrichment/apis/kill_chain_engine.py` is the **5-layer engine** used by **`GET /api/v1/killchain/scan`** and parts of brief construction — **not** the same as “called by nothing” (it is called from `killchain.py` and brief fetchers). **Fixes to signal modifier behavior** belong in `compute_kill_chain` + `signals.py` injection; **fixes to 5-layer scan** belong in the engine/registry.

## Context Block 2 — The Gap

The **signals list endpoint** returns **trade signals** + optional **injected** `kill_chain_verdict` / `score` / `direction` on each item (`/signals/master`), **not** the full `layer_1/2/3` object tree. The **compute_kill_chain** dict **does** include `layer_1`, `layer_2`, `layer_3`. UI that only binds to `/api/v1/signals` without master injection or a dedicated KC endpoint will **not** show layers unless those fields are added to the API or the UI calls `/kill-chain` / `KillChainDashboard` path.

## Context Block 3 — Stated “Current Live Values”

Treat as **hypothesis / narrative** unless re-verified on your session: numbers in that block may drift from PROBE outputs (e.g. specs net −80,891 vs −113,057). **PROBE 2** shows `entry_price` **650.73** (not `$0.00`) for this workspace snapshot.

## Context Block 4 — Economic Layer

ADP / GDPNow may exist in `/api/v1/brief/master`; **PROBE 5** confirms `TodaysBrief.tsx` and `MasterBriefPanels.tsx` do not reference `adp_prediction` / `gdp_nowcast` by key name — any rendering would need explicit components/hooks.

## Context Block 5 — Missing Layer

No `iran_geopolitical.py` surfaced in probes; **PROBE 9** shows `iran` / `geopolitical` strings in trump/enrichment code, **not** a dedicated Hormuz override module. `hormuz` / `macro_override` strings were **absent** in code search.

